===Funerals===
To the Ānists, a corpse must be treated with utmost respect to not insult God who created humans in his own image. Consequently, specific funeral rites are to be followed. The corpse must first be bathed, completely nude, followed by embalming and prayer. The corpse is then enshrouded and buried in a cemetery. The corpse must face upward, towards the sky and God, and burying a corpse with its face towards the ground is a great insult. 

